<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Commune of Piacenza</h1><p class="st-meta">1126 CE – 1336 CE (approx.) · capital Piacenza</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Po crossing city-republic whose merchants and bankers traded across Europe and whose Gothic town hall still dominates its main square.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Piacenza, an old Roman colony where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/via-aemilia">Via Emilia</a> meets the Po, had consuls by 1126. Its citizens took over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>'s powers and controlled the river crossings and the road to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-genoa">Genoa</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Governed by consuls and later a podestà, Piacenza joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lombard-league">Lombard League</a>, and the preliminary talks for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-constance">Peace of Constance</a> were held there in 1183. Its merchants and money-changers were active at the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-champagne">Champagne</a> fairs and in papal finance. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palazzo-gotico">Palazzo Gotico</a>, the town hall, was begun in 1281. Ghibelline lords such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uberto-pallavicino">Uberto Pallavicino</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alberto-scotti">Alberto Scotti</a> held power in the 13th century.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Rival families repeatedly invited outside lords, and in 1336 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azzone-visconti">Azzone Visconti</a> took the city into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-milan">Lordship of Milan</a>. Piacenza later became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-parma-and-piacenza">Duchy of Parma and Piacenza</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1126 CE – 1336 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:82.11%;width:4.18%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1126 CE – 1336 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Piacenza</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Uberto Pallavicino, Alberto Scotti</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Emilian, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Piacenza</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1231&amp;focus=commune-of-piacenza" aria-label="Commune of Piacenza on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4911 587 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Commune of Piacenza lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5231 843L5218 830"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5218 830h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5231 843h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5231 843h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Piacenza. <a href="/atlas?year=1231&amp;focus=commune-of-piacenza">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

